WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.807
"Restoring Our Natural GLP-1
Satiety Circuit with Fiber"

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:10.577
L-cells, the specialized cells
lining our digestive tract

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.379
that produce
appetite-suppressing hormones

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:15.949
like GLP-1, have receptors
on their surface

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:20.254
that respond to carbohydrates,
proteins, and fats,

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:22.222
as well as detect
bitter compounds

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.659
like quinine in tonic water
that I’ve talked about before,

00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:27.027
as well as pungent molecules,

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.963
as I detailed
in my video on spices.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:33.166
But if these cells churn out
appetite-suppressing hormones

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:36.670
in response to detecting carbs,
proteins, and fats,

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.739
why do we have
an obesity epidemic?

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:41.975
Why are so many people
gaining so much weight?

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:46.113
The problem is the majority
of GLP-1-producing L cells

00:00:46.113 --> 00:00:49.316
are located at the lower part
of our digestive tract,

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:51.518
way at the end
of our small intestine,

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:55.255
known as the distal ileum,
and especially in our colon.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.624
Unfortunately, the majority
of digested nutrients

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.559
are absorbed
in the upper GI tract

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.161
high in our small intestines,

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.597
so don’t reach
the distal ileum and colon

00:01:03.597 --> 00:01:05.799
where L-cells
are highly abundant,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:10.003
and so, we may rarely activate
a natural satiety mechanism

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.473
known as the ileal brake,
which you may remember

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.310
from my Evidence-Based
Weight Loss presentation.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.246
The ileal brake is the
intestinal feedback mechanism

00:01:19.246 --> 00:01:21.715
that tamps down our hunger.

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:23.951
As soon as calories
reach the ilium,

00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:26.753
the end of our small intestine,
L-cells are activated,

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.722
and GLP-1 is produced,

00:01:28.722 --> 00:01:31.858
which puts the brakes
on eating more.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.226
Our appetite is dialed down,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.263
and the rate at which food
leaves our stomach slows.

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:38.031
This can be shown
experimentally.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.667
If you insert a 9-foot tube
down people’s throats

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.503
and drip in any calories,
fat, protein, or sugar,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.973
you can activate
the ileal brake.

00:01:45.973 --> 00:01:48.241
Then, when they sit down
to an all-you-can-eat meal,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.544
(compared to individuals
in the placebo group

00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:53.213
who had just gotten a squirt
of water through the tube),

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.749
they eat
over 100 calories less.

00:01:55.749 --> 00:01:58.485
With the ileal brake on,
you just don’t feel as hungry.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.121
You feel just as full,
eating significantly less.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.091
That’s the ileal brake
in action.

00:02:04.091 --> 00:02:07.894
But our natural GLP-1
satiety mechanism fails,

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.564
because most food components
are rapidly digested

00:02:10.564 --> 00:02:13.166
and absorbed at the beginning
of our small intestine

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.502
and don’t make it down to
the end of the small intestine

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:18.739
where our GLP-1 secreting cells
are concentrated.

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:21.108
Well, that’s dumb.

00:02:21.108 --> 00:02:24.778
Why would our body design
an appetite regulation system

00:02:24.778 --> 00:02:27.614
based on calories
ending up in our colon,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.050
when most calories
get absorbed way before that

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.085
no matter how much we eat?

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.788
Because when we were evolving,

00:02:34.788 --> 00:02:38.058
there was no such thing
as table sugar.

00:02:38.058 --> 00:02:39.659
There was no such thing
as Wonder Bread.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.695
No such thing as vegetable oil.

00:02:41.695 --> 00:02:45.365
For the millions of years before
we began to sharpen spears,

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.035
mill grains, or boil sugarcane,

00:02:48.035 --> 00:02:50.370
our entire physiology
is presumed to have evolved

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.774
in the context of eating
what our great ape cousins did,

00:02:53.774 --> 00:02:58.245
a diet comprised of leaves,
roots, fruits, and nuts.

00:02:58.245 --> 00:03:01.515
W e started using tools
during the Paleolithic period,

00:03:01.515 --> 00:03:04.184
which only goes back
about two million years,

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.919
but we and other great apes
have been evolving

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.454
since the Miocene era,

00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:10.657
which goes back as far
as 20 million years.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.592
So, for as much
as the first 90 percent

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.261
of our hominoid existence,

00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:18.331
our body evolved
on mostly whole plant foods.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.100
Here’s why that matters.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.770
Animal cells are encased only
in easily digestible membranes,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.306
which allow the enzymes
in our gut to effortlessly

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:29.509
liberate the calories
within a steak, for example.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.777
Plant cells,
on the other hand,

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.413
have cell walls
that are made out of fiber,

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:36.216
which acts as an indigestible
physical barrier;

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.518
so, many of those calories
remain trapped

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:42.355
until the good gut bugs
in our colon eat that fiber

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.424
and spill out the contents
of plant cells

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.294
to signal GLP-1 release.

00:03:47.294 --> 00:03:50.697
When we get our calories,
our protein, fat, and carbs

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.500
(like the sugars in milk)
from animal foods,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.268
they get absorbed early
in the small intestine

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.004
and never get to activate
many of the satiety cells

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.840
that secrete GLP-1 hormones,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.042
which are
concentrated farther down.

00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:05.645
It’s the same when you consume
processed plant foods.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.648
Chug down sugar water,
white flour, and oil,

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.851
and the exact same thing
happens.

00:04:10.851 --> 00:04:13.920
But what if you walled off
your calories,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.021
in other words,
tried to make sure

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.890
as many of your calories
as possible,

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.458
your protein, your carbs,
your fat,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.993
were encased in cell walls?

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:24.030
In other words,
from whole, intact, plant foods?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.600
Let’s say you eat a nut.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.536
No matter how well you chew,
tiny bits of nut

00:04:29.536 --> 00:04:32.105
containing hundreds
of thousands of intact cells

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.874
are going to make it
down to your colon,

00:04:33.874 --> 00:04:36.810
where the fat can be released
by fiber-eating bacteria

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.179
to activate GLP-1 secretion.

00:04:39.179 --> 00:04:41.381
You can see the bacteria
breaking into the cells

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:44.084
and nom-nomming
all the goodies.

00:04:44.084 --> 00:04:47.821
The same happens when you eat
an apple or steel-cut oats.

00:04:47.821 --> 00:04:48.955
Instead of all the sugar
and starch

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.457
getting absorbed earlier,

00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:53.727
like if you drank apple juice
or ate a cracker,

00:04:53.727 --> 00:04:56.062
some of the carbs
spill out further down

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.632
to activate
your satiety hormones.

00:04:58.632 --> 00:05:00.767
Even though the milling
of whole grains into flour

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.470
can break open
all the grains’ cell walls,

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.839
whole-grain bread is still
better than white bread,

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:08.175
because whole-grain
at least has extra fiber

00:05:08.175 --> 00:05:09.776
that makes it
down to our colon.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:12.045
There, our good gut bugs
can turn the fiber

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.281
into short-chain fatty acids

00:05:14.281 --> 00:05:17.417
that can activate GLP-1
secretion on their own.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.753
And, fiber has
a gelling property

00:05:19.753 --> 00:05:21.488
that can trap
other calories in the meal

00:05:21.488 --> 00:05:24.858
and pull them farther down
the intestine.

00:05:24.858 --> 00:05:26.693
Chug a third-of-a-cup
(80 ml) of oil

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.428
on a high-fiber diet,

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:31.598
and more than twice as much fat
makes it to your colon

00:05:31.598 --> 00:05:34.067
than when you have
the same amount of oil

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.602
on a low-fiber diet.

00:05:35.602 --> 00:05:37.904
In other words,
even if you ate a donut

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.940
on an otherwise
high-fiber diet,

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.509
some of the donut calories
could still make it far enough

00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:45.612
down to help dial down
your hunger.

00:05:45.612 --> 00:05:47.247
So, we have to make sure
our calories

00:05:47.247 --> 00:05:49.549
get all the way down to the end
of our small intestine

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:52.018
for a sustained
release of GLP-1.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.020
And dietary fiber
can help do that

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.823
by slowing the digestion
and absorption of the calories

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.558
we eat to maximize
their activity

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:01.494
in sustaining the secretion
of GLP-1.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:05.131
So, part of
the "slow digestion strategy"

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:07.133
to sustain GLP-1 secretion

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:11.104
is dietary fiber to slow down
the digestion of nutrients.

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:14.140
This strategy has been proposed
as a dietary approach

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.210
to mimic the function
of bariatric surgery.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.979
Because certain procedures
can entail

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:21.881
literally cutting out
part of your small intestine,

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:24.017
nutrients get dumped
further down,

00:06:24.017 --> 00:06:27.187
causing a big GLP-1
ileal brake response.

00:06:27.187 --> 00:06:31.758
So, the modern medical solution
to this mismatch

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:34.227
between the foods
we were built to eat,

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:36.963
that naturally activate
satiety circuits,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.633
and the processed junk
we’re now being sold,

00:06:39.633 --> 00:06:43.270
is to physically,
surgically change our anatomy

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:44.537
to force it to the end
of our gut,

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:47.507
or inject GLP-1 mimicking drugs,

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:51.177
so we get GLP-1 activation
regardless of what we eat.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:54.247
It’s funny, you’ll read
how "almost no nutrients"

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.916
make it down to where
the GLP-1 producing cells are,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.319
"under normal conditions."

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:03.923
But by "normal"
they mean donuts for breakfast.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:07.727
When, really,
normal-for-our-species

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.763
is eating
so many unprocessed plant foods

00:07:09.763 --> 00:07:11.898
that we’re knocking down
triple-digit grams

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:13.500
of fiber every day.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.736
That entails massive amounts
of whole plant foods.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:20.173
So, to restore
our natural satiety circuits,

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:22.642
we can go under the knife,
under the needle,

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:27.213
or just eat
the way nature intended.

